#====================================================================
# E260 — A fixed interpreter launcher must execute the validated fd
#====================================================================

id:                     E260
trigger_tool:           native-image|runtime|test_package
phase:                  runtime|testing
error_signature:        native-image.*(126|127)|fixed Python launcher selected a shell wrapper|not an ELF executable|validated Python path was replaced before exec

severity:               3
category:               jvm|native-image|launcher|security|toctou
match_keywords:         native-image, Python launcher, shell wrapper, ELF magic, fixed path, fexecve, descriptor, TOCTOU, exit 127
title:                  A fixed interpreter launcher must execute the validated file descriptor

root_cause:             A signed launcher that validates a fixed Python path but later executes the pathname separates the checked object from the executed object. An executable shell wrapper can pass stat plus X_OK, and a same-UID writer can atomically replace a real ELF after validation but before path-based exec.
affected_scope:         Signed C or C++ launchers that invoke a Python companion through fixed interpreter candidates on systems where PATH and shell fallback are outside the trusted execution boundary.
verification_cmd:       Run the launcher with a shell wrapper followed by a real ELF candidate, then replace the selected path after validation; require wrapper rejection, deterministic all-negative failure, and execution of only the retained validated descriptor.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           descriptor-bound-elf-launch
rec_description:        Keep the absolute allow-list, open each candidate read-only, bind path and open identities, require ELF magic, retain the descriptor through exec, and launch it with fexecve or an equivalent fd-bound API.
rec_command:            Add an open_elf_executable helper that returns a validated descriptor and pass that descriptor directly to fexecve.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      package-private-elf-interpreter
fallback_description:   Package a trusted ELF interpreter inside the same runtime closure when no stable fixed system interpreter exists.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          packaging-change

forbid_1_pattern:       execv\(python|execlp|execvp|system\(|popen\(|/bin/sh|PATH.*python
forbid_1_reason:        Shell fallback, PATH search, or path execution after validation defeats the fixed-interpreter trust boundary.
forbid_1_consequence:   The launcher can execute a different object from the one it validated or fail with opaque 126 or 127 status.

principles:             P017

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E083,E232
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E260.md
last_updated:           2026-08-08
source_event:           GraalVM 25.0.3 PR #3928 Native Image descriptor-bound launcher closure

authors:                2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
